{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e","id":566006,"title":"Hoping for some changes to Aten in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-23T20:42:33-07:00","id":566006,"title":"Hoping for some changes to Aten in 2e","content":"I hate to make one of my first posts here a ranty one, but I'm really really hoping that Aten and his servants get a bit of a rewrite in Scion 2e (when the time comes, of course; that won't be till Scion: God).<br /> Basing the Titan of Light on the original Egyptian monotheism, and then having him appropriate/possibly invent the later Abrahamic ones, was a cool idea. Creating that secret society of Catholics dedicated to Fatebinding Gods into Saints (or something like that), was also a cool idea. But then you actually travel to the Greater Titan Akhetaten, and oh wait! Every single one of all of its minions is a suicide bomber angel who can be bypassed either by shouting dogmatic slogans at it or debating it into submission on pointless theological points. Was the writer just working out some internal anger about Jews/Christians/Muslims? Because everything else about the presentation of the Titans in that book is awesome and makes me want to start a campaign right at God-level, and this one part is just so strangely bad. It's like depicting the MtAs Celestial Chorus as composed entirely of fundamentalist Christians. Who are also suicide bombers. And lobotomised.<br /> [/rant]<br /> Anyway this is also my first post. Hello everybody! I got into the WoDs, both C and N, via an older cousin who had a lot of the older game books. Then I sort of forgot about White Wolf games for a while, and then I just recently came back to discover that all their stuff is being handled by this great big wonderful transparent thing called Onyx Path and I want to play in all of the universes at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6592-mrbridger","name":"MrBridger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T13:01:33-07:00","id":576687,"title":"","content":"Awww, Aten is actually one of my favorite things in Scion. Precisely because the whole idea is irreverent, funny and fits the feel of the game perfectly. It`s not like the depiction of pagan gods is very accurate either, so it`s only natural that monotheism gets the same treatment. This game doesn`t take itself too seriously even when it`s being all deep and poetic about something. So Aten is supposed to be over-the-top. It`s supposed to make you snicker even in a dangerous situation - because yeah, suicide bomber angels. It is NOT supposed to be offensive. Just like the portrayal of Shiva or Odin is not supposed to be offensive to a pagan (facepalm-worthy? maaaybe). It`s a game. If Tlazolteotl is running around cleaning the sewers, then the entity behind the greatest organized monotheistic religions of the setting can be as crazy as necessary. Bring on the slogans. Bring on the cheese. Fundamentalists in the real world might be srz business whatever religion they belong to, but in Scion? You get to laugh and enjoy the madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T10:46:04-07:00","id":577493,"title":"","content":"&lt;checks watch&gt;<br /> Is it time for the Aten/YHWH conflation wars again?<br /> I have got to set an alarm for these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T08:00:21-07:00","id":578760,"title":"","content":"Maybe YHWH is an elaborate Fate construct separate from the Hebrew deity. What would the implications of worship going towards something that only exists because it's worshipped.<br /> <br /> In other news, does anybody know who Pantheon number 10 is? I'm still hoping the Caanite one is in at some point, but if the 10th Hero pantheon is good I might end up buying Origins right off the bat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:43:02-07:00","id":578874,"title":"","content":"Supposed to be revealed at GenCon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:52:41-07:00","id":578879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=578874#post578874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supposed to be revealed at GenCon</div> </div> </div> </div>Along with (some of?) Demigod and God's pantheons, according to Neall. Across Hero, Demigod and God, the total's expected to be 20 pantheons, with even more intended for KS stretch goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T13:48:33-07:00","id":579113,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping for a complete overhaul on titans in 2e not just Aten.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d really love it if we got some nuance and depth of character to these beings that have all the power, intelligence and history that most gods do and yet get boiled down to 'incomprehensible entities that just want things to go back to the way they were by killing all of their children and humanity'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T17:48:12-07:00","id":579297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=579113#post579113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping for a complete overhaul on titans in 2e not just Aten.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d really love it if we got some nuance and depth of character to these beings that have all the power, intelligence and history that most gods do and yet get boiled down to 'incomprehensible entities that just want things to go back to the way they were by killing all of their children and humanity'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that incomprehensible attribute and seeming lack of depth part of what defines them as Titans? They aren't supposed to HAVE ideas, because they ARE ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T19:57:52-07:00","id":579329,"title":"","content":"Ehn. I have seen a lot of people interested in the game approaching more the mythology, and the Titans of Greek myth pretty clearly had ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T20:13:52-07:00","id":579330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=576687#post576687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awww, Aten is actually one of my favorite things in Scion. Precisely because the whole idea is irreverent, funny and fits the feel of the game perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? I think most of the other Gods and Titans can be played straight if you want (Tlazolteotl can be many scarier things than a sewer worker).<br /> Just for an example, look at the various Titan realm quests in the Scion: God example adventure. Every Overworld is under siege. Donner has to parachute into Surtsey to defeat an army of fire giants with modern weaponry. Adonis has to steal moly from an army of giants. The Baronne has to <i>talk her whole pantheon out of committing suicide</i>. And Harsihar gets to... interrogate refugee Gods to see which one of them is going to shout &quot;Allahu akbar&quot; and blow up. Some of these can be serious or humorous (Donner's, Adonis's). Some can only be serious (Baronne's). But I can't imagine playing Harsihar's scenario seriously, and that's what bothers me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6592-mrbridger","name":"MrBridger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:23:12-07:00","id":583799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=579330#post579330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it? I think most of the other Gods and Titans can be played straight if you want (Tlazolteotl can be many scarier things than a sewer worker).<br /> Just for an example, look at the various Titan realm quests in the Scion: God example adventure. Every Overworld is under siege. Donner has to parachute into Surtsey to defeat an army of fire giants with modern weaponry. Adonis has to steal moly from an army of giants. The Baronne has to <i>talk her whole pantheon out of committing suicide</i>. And Harsihar gets to... interrogate refugee Gods to see which one of them is going to shout &quot;Allahu akbar&quot; and blow up. Some of these can be serious or humorous (Donner's, Adonis's). Some can only be serious (Baronne's). But I can't imagine playing Harsihar's scenario seriously, and that's what bothers me.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why choose between scary and funny when you can have both? Tragedy and comedy are not mutually exclusive. Laughter does not diminish the seriousness of a dangerous or dark situation. It does not devalue serious matters, it is an integral part of the world, and sometimes it happens at inappropriate times.<br /> Think about it. The Trojan War started because three goddesses wanted to be acknowledged as the prettiest, and Zeus couldn`t be bothered, and it sort of went downhill from there. Is it funny as hell? You bet it is. Does it diminish all the tragedy and bloodshed? No. Same goes for the famous episode when Ares and Aphrodite overreact to minor wounds they recieved from a mortal. That`s ridiculous. But neither Olympian becomes any less divine because if it. Even one of the greatest tragedies of all time - &quot;The Bacchae&quot; - will make the reader snicker more than once.<br /> <br /> Regarding the scenarios you mention, Horace actually has a terrible crisis on his hands. Brainwashing minions might not be a sophisticated or dignified strategy, but it certainly is more efficient than it seems. Especially if it can happen to pretty much anyone. The ridiculousness of an enemy does not make said enemy harmless. It just makes all the havoc they can wreak more surreal.<br /> <br /> Actually, surreal is a good term for Aten. Sanity just doesn`s work with him. So yes, this Titan can probably never be &quot;played straight&quot; (unless you go for &quot;obfuscating stupidity&quot;), mainly because it`s one of the most twisted beings in the setting. And it`s brand of madness is contagious - so be happy we can`t take him seriously. Because as long as he makes you laugh, as long as you see how little sense everything about him makes - you are free from him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T14:24:10-07:00","id":583832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=583799#post583799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Trojan War started because three goddesses wanted to be acknowledged as the prettiest, and Zeus couldn`t be bothered, and it sort of went downhill from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, less &quot;Couldn't be bothered&quot; and more &quot;Did not want to pick who's prettier; his wife, his daughter, or his aunt/(adopted)daughter/daughter-in-law/however the fuck Aphrodite is related to him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fucking Greek Gods and their fucked up eldritch tumbleweed of a family tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T07:39:55-07:00","id":584726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But then you actually travel to the Greater Titan Akhetaten, and oh wait! Every single one of all of its minions is a suicide bomber angel who can be bypassed either by shouting dogmatic slogans at it or debating it into submission on pointless theological points. Was the writer just working out some internal anger about Jews/Christians/Muslims? Because everything else about the presentation of the Titans in that book is awesome and makes me want to start a campaign right at God-level, and this one part is just so strangely bad. It's like depicting the MtAs Celestial Chorus as composed entirely of fundamentalist Christians. Who are also suicide bombers. And lobotomised </div> </div> </div>NWODs Atheist flavor is well known. Yeah, Aten is basically a writer taking out their frustrations of the Abrahamic Religions out on the story and forcing us all through the ride by making it canon. Most of the offensive things about other cultures and deities can be largely chalked up to ignorance and lack of historical understanding (The writers probably didn't like reading mythology, see the need to take out their frustrations with religion), but there is no way in hell that they didin't realize that brainwashed suicide bomber angels or brainwashed dogmatists who can only debate theological minutiae might be a tad insulting. It was intended to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:14:03-07:00","id":584751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=583799#post583799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ridiculousness of an enemy does not make said enemy harmless. It just makes all the havoc they can wreak more surreal.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.comicvine.com/squirrel-girl/4005-2488/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.comicvine.com/squirrel-girl/4005-2488/</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T18:18:16-07:00","id":586662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=584726#post584726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> NWODs Atheist flavor is well known. Yeah, Aten is basically a writer taking out their frustrations of the Abrahamic Religions out on the story and forcing us all through the ride by making it canon. Most of the offensive things about other cultures and deities can be largely chalked up to ignorance and lack of historical understanding (The writers probably didn't like reading mythology, see the need to take out their frustrations with religion), but there is no way in hell that they didin't realize that brainwashed suicide bomber angels or brainwashed dogmatists who can only debate theological minutiae might be a tad insulting. It was intended to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The underlying concept of the Aten followers isn't really a bad idea, it's just when you present that concept with no room for subtlety that it falls apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T08:17:58-07:00","id":587131,"title":"","content":"About as subtle as if the Orisha/Vodoo had lain around all day using drugs and not working?<br /> <br /> It was intended to be offensive because the writers was taking out his frustrations on the real world counterpart to their religions and (correctly) assumed that no one would call them on it because they are not a traditionally protected class like a minority is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T15:14:47-07:00","id":588508,"title":"","content":"Aaand this is why Aten discussions go nowhere. There is always conflation with YHWH and people take religion (especially their own) seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T15:44:17-07:00","id":588522,"title":"","content":"The book conflates him with Yahweh explicitly, there is an entire titan spawn oriented group of religious extremists trying to fate bond all the other gods into abrahamic roles and make them subservient to Aten, His suicide bomber angels are clearly references to Muslim extremists and being able to debate his servants into the ground with theological loopholes is quite obviously a tongue in cheek reference to the Abrahamic sects (Given the western audience, probably more christian than anything.) and their conflicting theories and doctrines.<br /> <br /> I'm not even a Christan (and never was), I'm a Germanic Pagan, but that doesn't mean I'm blind to the obvious writing on the walls. If they did that to say, The Hindu pantheon or the Aztecs the forum would be freaking the hell out. I know this because they actually did, albeit they have the shield of legitimate cultural ignorance to hide behind and claim it wasn't intentional (which it probably wasn't).<br /> <br /> I'm guessing the forum wasn't outraged because it likely hews more secular than not and many Forumites share those same grievances that the author has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:11:35-07:00","id":589377,"title":"","content":"Aten's on My List for 2e, although it's a pretty big list. I still enjoy the idea of him being the Titan who originated the concept of solipsistic monotheism, but I'd much prefer he be handled with a more deft and subtle touch. He's got a bit more room thanks to the new pantheons in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T18:22:34-07:00","id":589739,"title":"","content":"How do the new pantheons give him more room? I would think they would take room away from him, page-wise.<br /> And I want to clarify, I have no problem with Aten inventing monotheism*; I think it's a really cool idea. I just thought he and his minions were written really poorly, and since he's the sole avatar of Akhetaten, that wrecks an entire Greater Titan.<br /> <br /> (*Although if players are uncomfortable with the idea, the Storyteller can always remind them what &quot;light-bearer&quot; translates to in Latin.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6592-mrbridger","name":"MrBridger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T20:18:08-07:00","id":589829,"title":"","content":"Yes, Aten was poorly written. Sad fact: Most of Scion was poorly written.<br /> You can either modify what is currently there* and hope the new writers do a better job, or you can join the several previous forum posts arguing about if Aten (or, churlishly, this forum) is anti-christian.<br /> <br /> *I threw out most of what they wrote and cracked the books on Aten for my game. If the current version is a non-starter, I suggest you do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T00:08:31-07:00","id":589981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=589377#post589377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aten's on My List for 2e, although it's a pretty big list. I still enjoy the idea of him being the Titan who originated the concept of solipsistic monotheism, but I'd much prefer he be handled with a more deft and subtle touch. He's got a bit more room thanks to the new pantheons in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Is solipsistic monotheism here the same thing as exclusive monotheism (that is, the belief there are no other gods but Aten)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T00:18:26-07:00","id":590012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=589377#post589377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aten's on My List for 2e, although it's a pretty big list. I still enjoy the idea of him being the Titan who originated the concept of solipsistic monotheism, but I'd much prefer he be handled with a more deft and subtle touch. He's got a bit more room thanks to the new pantheons in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Is solipsistic monotheism here similar to exclusive monotheism (that is, the belief that there are no gods but Aten)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T05:29:07-07:00","id":590160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=589829#post589829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Aten was poorly written. Sad fact: Most of Scion was poorly written.<br /> You can either modify what is currently there* and hope the new writers do a better job, or you can join the several previous forum posts arguing about if Aten (or, churlishly, this forum) is anti-christian.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your going to make passive aggressive sniping of me, You can at least do the honor of writing an actual arguement in favor of your position and against mine. Especially if your going to publicly accuse me of ungentlemanly conduct, lest the universe implode from the irony.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T05:38:11-07:00","id":590163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=589981#post589981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Is solipsistic monotheism here the same thing as exclusive monotheism (that is, the belief there are no other gods but Aten)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, except there are demonstrably other Gods, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T08:09:25-07:00","id":590223,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting, via solipsistic monotheism, to have the minions/followers of Aten immune or protected from the powers of the other gods because they just do not accept that the other gods are divine beings:<br /> A) Zeus is not a god, but a normal person.<br /> B) Normal people cannot throw lightning. <br /> C) Zeus cannot throw lightning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T08:16:35-07:00","id":590227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/566006-hoping-for-some-changes-to-aten-in-2e?p=590160#post590160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your going to make passive aggressive sniping of me, You can at least do the honor of writing an actual arguement in favor of your position and against mine. Especially if your going to publicly accuse me of ungentlemanly conduct, lest the universe implode from the irony.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do not have to argue my point against yours. My point is that this has been done over many times in this forum and the previous one. Ranting about anti-Christian bias and imparting a hatred of Christianity upon the writers (and through your other comments, this forum) helps nothing. Nor does it advance any new ideas.<br /> <br /> In the spirit of the original post in this thread, I must ask you: How would you change Aten to make him work in Scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T08:00:59-07:00","id":598354,"title":"","content":"The problem I had with Aten is that he appeared without warning.<br /> Scion Hero brushes off the Titans as unimportant at this stage in the story, but Monotheism being the byproduct of one of their enemies seems like a huge glaring thing for all of the gods you meet to consider totally unimportant. Yes, there's a story to be told with a character who discovered they were a Demigod but maintained their belief in a higher power only to learn it's the enemy but it's something the player or at least the fucking Storyteller should've known about in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}